f people  recommend disintegration which actually  does sound really good so i'll probably  get to that one day too and uh this is  actually his fourth  um  short story collection now he has a very  distinctive  writing style it's almost kind of like i  almost want to say that it's sort of  like  it's kind of poetic it has like a  surreal bent to it it almost has a kind  of like like a dark neo noir type of  thing  and a lot of the stories particularly in  this collection come across very much  like  they're almost i don't even know i mean  yes they have there are horror stories  and they have horror aspects to them but  there's all kind of other stuff going on  there it's almost kind of like sci-fi  um some of them have like a dark fantasy  type or like a surrealist kind of bent  to them they remind me very much and  it's interesting because there's  actually a pretty extensive author's  notes um thing at the end where he kind  of like explains uh you know where the  ideas for the stories came from and i  always like when writers do that i like  i've done that in my own short story  collections because i wish more writers  would do that but oh well because i'm  interested in how authors got their  ideas so he actually goes quite a bit  into where he got the ideas for the  stories where they had previously  appeared because i think all the stories  i think there are 14 stories in here and  all of them previously appeared in other  collections some of them were like in  you know best horror of the year and  various other ones so these have all  been published before but now they're  all kind of like uh brought together  like compiled into one work see so he  actually did say that some of his  stories were inspired by  black mirror so if you like black mirror  if you like david lynch if you like  stuff like that um that kind of vibe i  think you'll really really dig this i  mean some of it it's weird because like  the first couple stories like i said his  writing style is very  i don't it's not like run-on sentences  necessarily but it is very  it's very evocative  and and dream-like i could that's a good  word and amorphous i think that's maybe  the word that came that kind of like  came to me when i was reading the first  couple of stories they're very so a lot  of the stories are not like concrete in  the sense that this happens that happens  that happens they're ones that you have  to  they're kind of like atmosphere mood and  you kind of have like stuff happens in  them but you really kind of have to like  pay attention to  what's going on because everything's not  spelled out um like i said i kind of  feel like black mirror is the thing that  a lot that some of these stories like  really reminded me of and like i said he  did say in the end that he really really  liked black mirror and he you know liked  particular uh episodes of that and some  of those like gave him ideas for for  this and like i said interestingly too  one of the stories in here he said was  actually inspired by david lynch's lost  highway so if you like that kind of  stuff if you really like just kind of  like you know concrete abc type horror  then this is probably not for you this  is very like i said it's very  poetically written it's very amorphous  some of the stories like  not really like very few of the stories  give you any easy answers a lot of the  stories are have to do with they kind of  have a sense of bleakness or desolation  to them there's kind of like you know a  lot of them are set like after the end  of the world or after aliens have taken  over or something like that even though  things are not necessarily spelled out  you know very like really clearly but  you still get a sense of what's going on  through  the descriptions i guess so they're very  like atmospheric and uh so yeah and so  like i said if that if you don't like  dig that kind of like surrealist sort of  style then probably you're not gonna  like it but i actually quite 