g  from because i'm reading this story and  i said man this kind of reminds me of  that um that movie moon with sam  rockwell in it and when i was reading  the author's notes at the end he said  that that was one of the moon and  annihilation uh were where he kind of  got the ideas for this so basically what  that story is about is there's a guy  and he's in this kind of concrete bunker  like there's like an apartment like  living quarters but he's working there  and he's supposedly like extracting  these really really valuable minerals  and so his job is basically you know you  go to the drill he takes the minerals  and you have to like separate them out  and weigh them and everything and he  does this every single day and he's not  supposed to leave the compound because  it's supposedly somewhere like on the  arctic waist so it's like freezing cold  outside  and it's almost you you get a sense like  as it goes on  because a lot of these stories like i  said are very  purgatorial that's a good word for them  where it's somebody who's kind of like  trapped in some loop and they can't  remember like how long they've been  there or you know what's going on  outside so this one's very much like  that like this guy is kind of like oh i  had this contract for x amount of days  like i said that's why it reminded me a  lot of moon and uh which is an awesome  movie if you haven't seen it by the way  but uh yeah so this story did remind me  of that and he's just like it's it's a  really boring job and he doesn't see  anybody the only person that he sees is  this woman named rebecca who shows up  every 30 days to you know check on what  he's doing and take his samples and all  that other kind of stuff and it's um  it's weird because it's they start kind  of developing like a friendship and then  sort of a romance but then there's other  stuff going on like sometimes he has  like sometimes there's a spider and like  sometimes there's a pet rabbit and  sometimes and like i said