e kid  you know what i mean and like as it goes  on like you know what why they're  measuring the kid what they need it for  and that one actually  i don't is this too much of a spoiler  that one actually kind of has sort of a  happy ending or at least a hopeful  ending most of these do not like i said  um a lot of these are very bleak kind of  desolate sort of stories a lot of them  are  you know people stuck in these kind of  like purgatorial loops uh perhaps of  their own making so it really has this  kind of  and like i said it does have a kind of  like neo-noir type of thing too it's  often called like transgressive fiction  they call it that too but it's just kind  of like this  you know it's it's really hard to  describe like the writing style but  if you know you know um this kind of  reminded me a little i have to say this  reminded me slightly  of if you guys remember like a while  back i reviewed another short story  collection which was wounds by nathan  balangrid and uh this kind of is like  that it's not not like exactly the same  but it's like a similar that's like a  similar sort of genre i guess if you  want to call it that so if you're really  into that book which like i said was  kind of like a surrealist  sort of thing  then you'd probably really really dig  this as well this is the first richard  thomas that i've read um he has like a  lot of like i said he's been in a [ __ ]  ton of short story like uh anthologies  he's done stuff with like uh chuck  palaniak who has a blurb here on the  cover so and also so if you like that  kind of stuff um just kind of weird  fiction in general then probably you  will really really dig this and you know  like i said and i only brought up like  three of the stories in there that stood  out to me the most but there are like  all pretty much all of these are pretty  awesome um those three were my favorite  ones but i mean the first story repent  is also uh pretty great so it's just  it's just a really good  creepy  unsettling  kind of like i said surrealist sort of  uh stories and they all kind of have i  mean they're all different and they all  have like different stories but they all  have kind of like  um similar themes to them so the so the  collection really does hang together  quite well even though the stories i  believe were written over like a  five-year time period uh you know and  appeared in various anthologies and some  of this stuff was written  with specific uh things in mind like uh  there was a couple stories in here that  are kind of  nominally about clowns sort of  um one in particular is about this clown  named crinkles but the reason that he  wrote that was because there was an  another anthology like a multi-author  anthology who  and it was kind of all set in the same  world about this character crinkles the  clown but he went like really strange  with it like really cosmic  um there's also like a couple of sort of  like lovecraftian stories in here one in  particular which is called in his house  which is you know straight up  lovecraftian uh and it's also kind of  written in sort of like an epistolary  style as though it's a letter addressed  to you the reader um and i also quite  liked that one as well but yeah  definitely uh check this out like i said  this is uh it'll be out in february of  2022. i believe you can pre-order it at  the moment on amazon and there's a  couple of um  of kind of big like publishers weekly  and stuff like that have already  reviewed it so like i said they've been  sending out advanced readers copy of  which uh i got one right here like i  said advanced reader's crappy i feel so  special but uh yeah so definitely if you  like i said if you dig black mirror or  like any kind of surrealist neo noir  type fiction then you definitely need to  check this out because this will be  right up your alley so yeah that'll do  it for this tomes of terror and i will  be back on the next one bye

